{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-330661",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/8a6467813ccf982906fb5d1d8cd5c5c88b984c22a1e238715c65315a7772249c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=\u03a6(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ee2aebec9953a09dca6eab5c7e5434240885a383a6701638fffdaa9ee9cfeb40.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.38).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/619fae52bde8b2da729095f733e1ea1411132fffe70cc23e252a83cbb2e7ff23.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.38) & =P(Z>0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.38) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.6480 \\\\  & =0.3520.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
